samsung-ml2160-rust (2.0.0~alpha-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Suppress system-config-printer's duplicate USB queue creation for the
    hardware-confirmed Samsung 04e8:330f device. Keep the existing IPP queue
    and preserve automatic setup for other USB devices.
  * Reload udev rules on installation/removal without replaying device events.
    Existing legacy queues must be removed explicitly by the administrator.
  * Document successful hardware printing and CUPS network sharing, and the
    duplicate queue observed on Debian testing with GNOME.

 -- Çağan ERGÜN <caganergun@tutanota.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0300

samsung-ml2160-rust (2.0.0~alpha-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The package is now the printer application, not the CUPS filter. It
    installs /usr/bin/ml216x-printer-app and a systemd unit that runs it as a
    system service on the loopback address; it installs no filter and no PPD,
    which is decision Q-5's clean break for what we ship. The 1.x filter and
    the PPD stay in the source tree.
  * Dynamically linked against the archive's libpappl and glibc, so the musl
    static build is gone (decisions Q-1 and Q-7). Dependencies are stated
    explicitly rather than through ${shlibs:Depends}, which nothing in this
    build path would ever substitute; they were derived from the binary and
    cross-checked with dpkg-shlibdeps.
  * Built by scripts/build-deb.sh, which checks the libpappl version range
    before building rather than only declaring it.

 -- Çağan ERGÜN <caganergun@tutanota.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 18:20:00 +0300

samsung-ml2160-rust (2.0.0~alpha-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Open the 2.0 development line. The 1.x CUPS raster filter is frozen at
    1.0.2 on the legacy/cups-filter-1.x branch; work on main moves to a
    standalone Printer Application. No functional change in this entry.

